Sometimes when you ask her,

597
00:17:28,040 --> 00:17:28,400
she won't say.

598
00:17:28,400 --> 00:17:29,600
She doesn't bring things up
with us either.

599
00:17:29,600 --> 00:17:30,440
If she can hold things in,

600
00:17:30,440 --> 00:17:31,120
then comparatively,

601
00:17:31,120 --> 00:17:32,480
you're like that too.

602
00:17:32,960 --> 00:17:33,480
She rubs off on me.

603
00:17:33,480 --> 00:17:34,680
Now I hold things in too.

604
00:17:36,200 --> 00:17:37,080
Do you like doing that?

605
00:17:38,760 --> 00:17:40,240
Depends who I'm talking to.

606
00:17:40,240 --> 00:17:41,040
Because sometimes,

607
00:17:41,040 --> 00:17:41,800
saying too much

608
00:17:41,800 --> 00:17:42,560
can feel

609
00:17:42,560 --> 00:17:43,680
like a burden.

610
00:17:44,680 --> 00:17:45,160
Yeah.

611
00:17:46,520 --> 00:17:47,360
Like when

612
00:17:47,360 --> 00:17:48,840
Fang and I talk,

613
00:17:48,840 --> 00:17:50,480
I don't feel any pressure.

614
00:17:51,200 --> 00:17:52,080
I can just

615
00:17:52,080 --> 00:17:53,520
say whatever I want.

616
00:18:04,800 --> 00:18:06,000
Facing the sea...

617
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:07,200
With spring blossoms all around.

618
00:18:07,680 --> 00:18:08,600
When I look at the sea,

619
00:18:08,600 --> 00:18:09,800
I don't overthink things.

620
00:18:09,800 --> 00:18:10,800
It just feels great.

621
00:18:11,560 --> 00:18:13,960
Before the waves reach you,

622
00:18:13,960 --> 00:18:15,120
you can see them coming.

623
00:18:15,760 --> 00:18:17,440
One after another.

624
00:18:17,440 --> 00:18:18,360
Yeah.

625
00:18:18,360 --> 00:18:18,960
I find that

626
00:18:18,960 --> 00:18:21,200
really interesting.

627
00:18:24,720 --> 00:18:26,240
It feels like it'd be hard

628
00:18:26,240 --> 00:18:27,160
to be unhappy living on an island.

629
00:18:27,880 --> 00:18:30,040
You get so much sunlight every day.

630
00:18:30,040 --> 00:18:30,880
Yeah.

631
00:18:33,040 --> 00:18:35,360
If you could choose

632
00:18:35,360 --> 00:18:38,200
your "evolution path",

633
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:39,560
would you rather grow wings first

634
00:18:39,560 --> 00:18:40,960
or gills?

635
00:18:42,240 --> 00:18:43,640
Would you rather

636
00:18:43,640 --> 00:18:45,120
explore the sky first

637
00:18:45,120 --> 00:18:46,640
or the ocean?

638
00:18:47,040 --> 00:18:48,120
Gills.

639
00:18:48,120 --> 00:18:49,040
What about you?

640
00:18:49,240 --> 00:18:50,720
If I didn't have

641
00:18:50,720 --> 00:18:52,520
to consider real life, gills.

642
00:18:52,520 --> 00:18:53,480
But realistically,

643
00:18:53,480 --> 00:18:54,280
I'd choose wings.

644
00:18:56,160 --> 00:18:57,760
It'd make commuting easier.

645
00:18:58,040 --> 00:18:59,200
But honestly,

646
00:18:59,200 --> 00:19:00,640
you could have

647
00:19:00,640 --> 00:19:01,680
your own home underwater.

648
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:03,000
If you have gills,

649
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:05,560
then you wouldn't need to worry

650
00:19:05,560 --> 00:19:06,840
about commuting on land.

651
00:19:08,120 --> 00:19:09,560
That's true.

652
00:19:09,560 --> 00:19:10,520
Gills alone wouldn't be enough.

653
00:19:10,520 --> 00:19:11,560
I'd also need

654
00:19:11,560 --> 00:19:12,880
a super strong body.

655
00:19:12,880 --> 00:19:13,720
Yeah.

656
00:19:13,720 --> 00:19:15,240
And I'd need the ability

657
00:19:15,240 --> 00:19:16,760
to move really fast underwater.

658
00:19:16,760 --> 00:19:17,480
Right.

659
00:19:17,480 --> 00:19:19,480
Ideally up to

660
00:19:19,480 --> 00:19:20,480
640 kilometers an hour.

661
00:19:21,680 --> 00:19:23,320
Then I could swim for
about half an hour every day

662
00:19:23,320 --> 00:19:25,680
and get pretty far.

663
00:19:30,200 --> 00:19:32,040
Let's think of something
that fits the scenery.

664
00:19:32,040 --> 00:19:34,200
What does this remind you of?

665
00:19:34,200 --> 00:19:35,840
What comes to your mind?

666
00:19:36,280 --> 00:19:38,200
Withered vines, old trees
and evening crows...

667
00:19:38,200 --> 00:19:39,760
A little bridge and a flowing stream.

668
00:19:41,800 --> 00:19:43,720
That doesn't quite fit.

669
00:19:43,720 --> 00:19:46,240
But "the setting sun" does.

670
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:47,680
That's okay.

671
00:19:47,680 --> 00:19:50,680
The sun also rises.

672
00:19:51,460 --> 00:19:53,180
(Laughs)

673
00:19:57,240 --> 00:19:58,800
Let's go eat.

674
00:19:58,800 --> 00:19:59,480
Let's go.

675
00:20:00,960 --> 00:20:01,720
Have a seat.

676
00:20:01,720 --> 00:20:02,520
Okay.

677
00:20:02,520 --> 00:20:03,160
Where are you sitting?

678
00:20:03,160 --> 00:20:03,920
Over here.

679
00:20:04,920 --> 00:20:05,920
Where are you sitting?

680
00:20:05,920 --> 00:20:07,720
Then I guess I can only sit here.

681
00:20:07,720 --> 00:20:08,520
Okay.

682
00:20:09,120 --> 00:20:10,000
Have a seat.

683
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:11,240
Alright.

684
00:20:17,320 --> 00:20:19,120
Guess what we're eating.

685
00:20:19,120 --> 00:20:20,040
Thai food.

686
00:20:20,060 --> 00:20:21,020
(Teasing)

687
00:20:23,840 --> 00:20:25,440
That is the safest answer.

688
00:20:26,960 --> 00:20:29,080
The safest answer.

689
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:32,640
Don't you think

690
00:20:32,640 --> 00:20:33,720
I'm someone

691
00:20:33,720 --> 00:20:35,080
who makes people feel at ease?

692
00:20:35,760 --> 00:20:37,480
(Imitating)
Yes, that's your gift.

693
00:20:38,840 --> 00:20:40,240
I said it before back when we were

694
00:20:40,240 --> 00:20:41,200
in the house gym.

695
00:20:41,200 --> 00:20:42,800
I said talking to you

696
00:20:42,800 --> 00:20:44,000
felt really easy and pleasant.

697
00:20:44,960 --> 00:20:48,000
That's where your wisdom lies.

698
00:20:48,960 --> 00:20:49,920
Thank you.

699
00:20:52,080 --> 00:20:52,960
Thank you.

700
00:20:54,600 --> 00:20:55,280
Thank you.

701
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:56,640
Can you reach it?

702
00:20:56,700 --> 00:20:58,480
(Switching places)

703
00:20:58,480 --> 00:20:59,360
Yeah.

704
00:20:59,360 --> 00:21:00,040
Thanks.

705
00:21:00,040 --> 00:21:01,320
No problem. Let's eat.

706
00:21:01,320 --> 00:21:01,760
It's...

707
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:02,360
Yeah, let's.

708
00:21:02,360 --> 00:21:03,360
I'm getting hungry.

709
00:21:03,360 --> 00:21:04,480
I can't wait anymore.

710
00:21:04,480 --> 00:21:05,200
Yeah.

711
00:21:05,200 --> 00:21:06,240
Try this.

712
00:21:06,240 --> 00:21:07,000
It's really good.

713
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:07,520
Really?

714
00:21:07,520 --> 00:21:08,720
You have to dip it in the sauce.

715
00:21:08,720 --> 00:21:09,680
Let me try.

716
00:21:14,920 --> 00:21:15,440
Right?

717
00:21:16,800 --> 00:21:18,040
Watch your sleeve.

718
00:21:18,680 --> 00:21:19,520
Thanks.

719
00:21:21,440 --> 00:21:22,440
This is so satisfying.

720
00:21:22,440 --> 00:21:23,400
My ideal plan

721
00:21:23,400 --> 00:21:24,680
for today

722
00:21:24,680 --> 00:21:25,840
was to see the ocean first,

723
00:21:25,840 --> 00:21:27,240
then hit the night market.

724
00:21:27,600 --> 00:21:28,400
I didn't expect the food

725
00:21:28,400 --> 00:21:29,440
to be this good.

726
00:21:29,440 --> 00:21:30,200
It really is.

727
00:21:30,200 --> 00:21:31,160
Have you noticed

728
00:21:31,160 --> 00:21:31,880
that once you learn to cook,

729
00:21:31,880 --> 00:21:32,800
you become less picky?

730
00:21:32,800 --> 00:21:33,800
Actually, yeah.

731
00:21:33,800 --> 00:21:34,320
Why is that?

732
00:21:34,320 --> 00:21:35,160
Good question.

733
00:21:36,480 --> 00:21:37,880
Before university,

734
00:21:37,880 --> 00:21:39,120
I used to cook too.

735
00:21:39,120 --> 00:21:40,520
But whenever a recipe said

736
00:21:40,520 --> 00:21:41,680
I had to add scallions,
ginger, and garlic,

737
00:21:41,680 --> 00:21:42,400
I'd refuse.

738
00:21:42,400 --> 00:21:43,040
I wouldn't add them.

739
00:21:43,040 --> 00:21:44,080
I'd just go for the original flavor.

740
00:21:44,760 --> 00:21:45,240
Later I realized

741
00:21:45,240 --> 00:21:46,360
it actually tastes much better
with them.

742
00:21:46,680 --> 00:21:47,720
You're hilarious.

743
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:49,880
Do you think

744
00:21:49,880 --> 00:21:51,360
you're one of a kind?

745
00:21:53,160 --> 00:21:54,840
Must you raise your eyebrows twice
when you say that?

746
00:21:54,840 --> 00:21:55,640
(Imitating)
One of a kind.

747
00:22:00,080 --> 00:22:02,320
I feel like I've been eating a lot more
these past two days.

748
00:22:02,320 --> 00:22:03,440
Me too.

749
00:22:03,440 --> 00:22:05,320
Everything here
really whets your appetite.

750
00:22:05,320 --> 00:22:05,880
It's sweet and sour.

751
00:22:06,680 --> 00:22:07,760
My appetite's gotten better.

752
00:22:07,760 --> 00:22:08,720
It's so good.

753
00:22:08,720 --> 00:22:09,600
The more I eat, the hungrier I get.

754
00:22:09,600 --> 00:22:10,400
It feels like...

755
00:22:10,400 --> 00:22:12,320
We can seriously eat a lot.

756
00:22:12,320 --> 00:22:13,880
I haven't felt

757
00:22:13,880 --> 00:22:14,720
this hungry in ages.

758
00:22:14,720 --> 00:22:15,960
Your appetite is contagious.

759
00:22:15,960 --> 00:22:17,320
Whenever I eat with you,

760
00:22:17,320 --> 00:22:18,680
I suddenly want to eat more.

761
00:22:18,680 --> 00:22:20,440
(Amused)
My appetite is contagious?

762
00:22:20,440 --> 00:22:23,160
I saved all this for you.

763
00:22:23,160 --> 00:22:24,200
Eat up. Thanks.

764
00:22:24,200 --> 00:22:25,200
This is for you too.

765
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:27,280
Have this.

766
00:22:27,280 --> 00:22:28,280
And this one too,

767
00:22:28,280 --> 00:22:29,120
even though I love eating too.

768
00:22:29,820 --> 00:22:31,140
(Smiles)

769
00:22:37,860 --> 00:22:39,900
(Don't go anywhere. The next episode
is even more romantic.)
